Until the prescanner exists, -E prints its input unchanged, with or without
-fopenmp, through the driver or straight through -fc1.

RUN: merkc -E %S/Inputs/sumsq.m -o %t && diff %S/Inputs/sumsq.m %t
RUN: merkc -E -fopenmp %S/Inputs/sumsq.m -o %t.omp && diff %S/Inputs/sumsq.m %t.omp
RUN: merkc -fc1 -E %S/Inputs/sumsq.m -o %t.fc1 && diff %S/Inputs/sumsq.m %t.fc1
RUN: merkc -E - < %S/Inputs/sumsq.m | diff %S/Inputs/sumsq.m -

RUN: merkc -E %S/Inputs/sumsq.m | FileCheck %s
CHECK:      :- module sumsq.
CHECK:      sum_squares(A, N, Sum) :-
CHECK-NEXT:     %$omp parallel do reduction(+)
CHECK-NEXT:     int.fold_up(add_square(A), 0, N, 0, Sum).

Line endings and a byte order mark are kept exactly, and no final newline is
added.
RUN: printf '\357\273\277:- module m.\r\n:- interface.' > %t.crlf.m
RUN: merkc -E %t.crlf.m -o %t.crlf.out && cmp %t.crlf.m %t.crlf.out
